          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} duality in string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effect"} non-perturbative
            enhancement of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+heterotic+and+type+II+string+theory"} duality between heterotic and type II string theory
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"}> KK-compactified
            ” on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptically fibered
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3"} K3
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            is supposed to be equivalent to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactified
            on a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-torus"} 2-torus
          %p
            More generally,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            fibered
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to B
            with elliptic
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3"} K3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            is supposed to be equivalent to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptically fibered
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Yau+manifold"} Calabi-Yau manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z \to B
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
          %p
            A detailed discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            of the respective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces"} moduli spaces
            is originally due to (
            %a{:href => "#FriedmanMorganWitten97"}> Friedman-Morgan-Witten 97
            ). A review of this is in (
            %a{:href => "#Donagi98"}> Donagi 98
            ).
          %p
            From the abstract of (
            %a{:href => "#Donagi98"}> Donagi 98
            ).
          %blockquote
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} compactified
              on an
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptically fibered
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Yau+variety"} Calabi-Yau
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z \to B
              is conjectured to be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} dual
              to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} compactified
              on an
              = succeed "-dimensional" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Yau+variety"} Calabi-Yau
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to B
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3"} K3
              fibers. In particular, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli"} moduli
              of the two theories should be
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=2
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} compactification
              is to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimensions"} dimensions
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo =
                      %mn 8
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d=8
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 6
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 6
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4
              respectively. Mathematically, the richest picture seems to emerge for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=3
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
              involves an analytically
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrable+system"} integrable system
              whose fibers admit rather different descriptions in the two theories.
          %h2#aspects Aspects
          %h3#SingularLocusAndD7Branes Singular locus of the elliptic fibration and 24 D7-branes
          %p
            In passing from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+monopole"} Kaluza-Klein monopole
            in 11d becomes the locus of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
            in 10d. The locus of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+monopole"} Kaluza-Klein monopole
            in turn (as discussed there) is the locus where the
            = succeed "-circle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1_A
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mi B
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1_A \times S^1_B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptic fibration
            degenerates to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nodal+curve"} nodal curve
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-dual
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D7-branes"} D7-branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D7-branes"} D7-branes
            in F-theory “are” the singular locus of the elliptic fibration.
          %p
            Now an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptically+fibered+complex+K3-surface"} elliptically fibered complex K3-surface
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi K
                          %mn 3
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℂ
                          %msup
                            %mi ℙ
                            %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  T &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; K3
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbb{C}\mathbb{P}^1
                  }
          %p
            may be parameterized via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weierstrass+elliptic+function"} Weierstrass elliptic function
            as the solution locus of the equation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi y
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 3
                  %mo +
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  y^2 = x^3 + f(z) x + g(z)
          %p
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi ℙ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y,z \in \mathbb{C}\mathbb{P}^1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial"} polynomial
            of degree 8 and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            of degree twelve. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/j-invariant"} j-invariant
            of the complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
            which this parameterizes for given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 24
                      %mi f
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mn 3
                    %mrow
                      %mn 27
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mn 2
                      %mo +
                      %mn 4
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mn 3
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  j(\tau(z)) = \frac{4 (24 f)^3}{27 g^2 + 4 f^3}
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poles"} poles
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo →
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j\to \infty
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/j-invariant"} j-invariant
            correspond to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nodal+curve"} nodal curve
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D7-branes"} D7-branes
            are located.
          .float_right_image{:style => "margin: -40px 0px 20px 20px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:alt => "homotopy pasting diagram exhibiting the homotopy Whitehead integral", :src => "/nlab/files/K3CobordismBetween24ThreeSpheres.jpg", :width => "260px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                from
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Equivariant+Cohomotopy+and+Oriented+Cohomology+Theory"} SS21
          %p
            Since the order of the poles is 24 (the polynomial degree of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discriminant"} discriminant
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 27
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mn 4
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta = 27 g^2 + 4 f^3
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptically+fibered+K3-surface"} elliptically fibered K3-surface
                –
                %a{:href => "elliptic+fibration+of+a+K3-surface#SingularPoints"} singular points
            %em 24 D7-branes
            (
            %a{:href => "#Sen96"}> Sen 96, page 5
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Sen97b"} Sen 97b
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Morrison04"} Morrison 04, sections 8 and 17
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Denef08"} Denef 08, around (3.41)
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "duality+between+M%2FF-theory+and+heterotic+string+theory#DouglasParkSchnell14"} Douglas-Park-Schnell 14
          %p
            Under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            this translates to 24
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA string theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3"} K3
            (
            %a{:href => "#Vafa96"}> Vafa 96, Footnote 2 on p. 6
            ).
          %p
            Notice that the
            %em net charge
            of these 24 D7-branes is supposed to vanish, due to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            effects (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Denef08"} Denef 08, below (3.41)
          %p
            (This reminds one of the situation for the
            = succeed "\u2026)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/third+stable+homotopy+group+of+spheres"} third stable homotopy group of spheres
          %p
            For analogous discussion of 24 NS5-branes in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3"} K3
            see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "duality+in+string+theory#Schwarz97"} Schwarz 97, around p. 50
          %p
            For more see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/24+branes+transverse+to+K3"} 24 branes transverse to K3
