          %h3#NonReducibleHeteroticGaugeBackgrounds
            Non-reducible heterotic
            = succeed "-gauge" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 8
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_8
          %p
            There are some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
            backgrounds whose supposed dual in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            involves an
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E8"} E8
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connection"} principal connection
            which is not
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduction+of+the+structure+group"} reducible
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SemiSpin%2816%29"} SemiSpin(16)
            (
            %a{:href => "#DistlerSharpe10"}> Distler-Sharpe 10, section 5
            ), while in fact the traditional construction of the heterotic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            theory only covers this case. In (
            %a{:href => "#DistlerSharpe10"}> Distler-Sharpe 10, section 7-8
            ) it is argued that therefore a more general formulation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            needs to involve
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+WZW+models"} parameterized WZW models
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory#GeneralGaugeBackgroundsAndParameterizedWZWModels"} heterotic string – Properties – General gauge backgrounds and parameterized WZW models
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
